# Styx @VERSION@ — Linux desktop

Share this computer with ChatGPT through an existing Gateway, or make this
computer the Gateway and share it too. Setup lets you choose which capabilities
this computer provides: commands, Browser Automation and Computer Use.

Extract the archive, enter its folder, and start installation:

```sh
cd @BUNDLE@
./install.sh
```

The installer keeps Styx in your user data directory, registers the `styx`
command, and opens terminal setup with the desktop role choices. After installation
you can remove the extracted folder; the installed program is retained separately.

Join an existing Gateway with its address and pairing code. A Host-only computer
does not need a separate Tunnel or ChatGPT connection. Setup also offers creating
a Gateway together with this Host. Computer Use needs an available desktop session
and the platform's normal permissions.

Styx uses your systemd user services and follows your desktop login lifecycle,
including when this computer also runs the Gateway. Desktop installation does
not enable systemd linger.

Use `styx quit` to stop Styx and `styx start` to start it again. To remove its
user services while retaining your configuration, run `styx uninstall`.
Install a newer package through its same `./install.sh` entry; the installer
updates an existing setup and preserves its configuration.
